  "inventoryReceipt": "The 24 iai cells in the retained profiles are the prereg inventory: five benefits (growth16_n/2n/4n, multiseg_cold_256k, seg_cycle_decommit_256k), four hot controls (small_churn_16b, churn_256b, churn_write_256b, aligned_churn_640b_a128), thirteen mimalloc cells, publication and producer; every cell appears once per arm label A1, A2, B1, B2, C0.",
  "nativeSharedAllocationPathReview": "native (production only) and twin (adds bench-internals+internals) are built from one example source. The twin adds only a read-only RouteDirectory/reservation geometry probe executed before the workers are spawned, outside the barrier window that is timed; the timed loop is the same std::alloc::dealloc through the installed #[global_allocator] SeferAlloc in both. Geometry copied from the twin to the native row is therefore an inference from a different binary, not independent ownership proof in the native binary; feature differences can move codegen. Native dispersion is wide (for example n=8 arm A min 280 ns/op, max 1019 ns/op over 18 runs), so the native axis is reviewed as noise-limited.",
  "producerProfileReview": "Raw child profiles of the producer cell reviewed for all five arm labels and their controls: every control has childIr = totalIr = 1 (the bare ret, equal in all five labels), every primary has childIr = totalIr (A1, A2, C0: 1515559; B1, B2: 1552551), one boundary execution and two thread profiles each; A1/A2/C0 and B1/B2 are bit-identical pairs. Oracle: B producer summary_load 4096 and summary_rmw 64, A producer both 0, pending words 0 in both, strict-trim consumed 4096 in both.",
